GNAT's exception personality routine, for the userland run-time system
(#170).

raise-gcc.c, raise.h and runtime.h are from GCC's gcc/ada directory, and
unwind-pe.h from libgcc, on the releases/gcc-15 branch, to match the GCC 15
compiler that builds Rose. They are unchanged. GCC installs the Ada run-time
system's Ada sources, but not these.

raise-gcc.c is compiled freestanding, with STANDALONE (which uses
runtime.h, and no C library), IN_RTS, and without C++ exception
interoperability (GXX_EH_INTEROP=0). stdlib.h is Rose's: the little of the
C library that raise-gcc.c includes.

The unwinder itself (unwind-dw2.o and unwind-dw2-fde-dip.o) comes from the
installed GCC's 32-bit libgcc_eh.a, and ../rose-unwind.c provides what it
needs from the C library.
